  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (Associate of Arts in Business intro, Bachelor of Arts in Business Economics, Bachelor of Arts in Business Information Systems, partial Bachelor of Arts in Business Leadership); the request did not name one, so this ledger covers the Bachelor of Arts in Business Economics, the first complete program in the capture. Confirm the intended program.",
    "ECO 204 (3 credits) also satisfies Global Campus Foundations requirements, but the capture does not say which specific Foundations course it replaces; the listed items therefore sum to 123 credits versus the 120-credit total.",
    "GEN 101 Developing Skills and Strategies for Success (3 credits) is scheduled first and counts toward elective credits, not Foundations; the capture does not state whether the 45 elective credits are reduced accordingly. GEN 104 likewise counts toward electives for students transferring in fewer than 30 credits.",
    "Foundations courses may be substituted; the capture lists only the standard sequence and does not specify which substitutions are allowed.",
    "The capture states a residency requirement of a minimum of 30 credits completed at the University, but it does not tie this to any specific course, so no requirement is marked institutional-only.",
    "A minimum of 30 upper-division credits, including 18 upper-division credits in the major, is required; the capture does not identify which electives must be upper-division.",
    "The capture does not state how the Quantitative Reasoning requirement (a prerequisite for BUS 308, BUS 401, and ECO 342) is met within the Foundations sequence."
  ],
